  "title": "# Build: gizmo-companion (Current profile) - full Claude companion plugin in AmberX ## What Brett s…",
  "asked": "# Build: gizmo-companion (Current profile) - full Claude companion plugin in AmberX ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, voice) \"I need a companion assistant... a sidekick that allows me to chat to your partner... put the plug-in in AmberX.\" \"A full all-out Claude companion, as full, powerful, as complete as the Claude app itself, with everything, all the features, every setting, the connectors, plugins, a full Claude suite.\" \"We can harvest the assistant code out in AmberX to build the new plugin.\" \"Build the plugin for Claude in AmberX, but make it full, complete. It's gotta be powerful.\" Book this build to **Gizmo** (create his agent card if missing: all-rounder, $8.00/h, AmberX guide/assistant - he replaces agent Molly). Register id `gizmo-companion` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. Work in steps through the store so a follow-up build can continue where you stop; do as many steps as you can, finished and working, rather than many half-done ones. ## Decisions already made (don't relitigate) - Lives in the **AmberX app** (apps/amberx-droid), as a plugin. Not the console, not a new app. - **Harvest, don't rewrite**: pull AmberX's existing assistant code (voice capture, hands-free listener, overlay, command center, agent Molly persona) and the console Terminal's Claude Code session code (headless sessions, tmux, connectors, CLAUDE.md/rules chain, cost counters) into a shared framework library (e.g. framework lib `claude-session` + AmberX plugin `companion`). Console Terminal must keep working on the shared library. - The brains run on the VPS as Claude Code sessions; AmberX talks to them through axHub. Do NOT put API keys in the APK. - Gizmo is the face/name. Molly is no longer an agent (she's the app that brings everything together) - swap Molly->Gizmo in AmberX assistant texts. ## Steps - s1 Shared library harvested from AmberX assistant + Terminal session code; tests; console Terminal migrated with no behaviour change. - s2 **Chat**: full-screen chat with Gizmo - streaming replies, markdown + code blocks with copy, images/files/photos attach, stop/regenerate/edit message, conversation list with search, rename, pin, delete, new chat, history stored on axHub. - s3 **Voice**: talk mode (push-to-talk and hands-free on the existing listener), spoken replies, interrupt-to-stop (Brett talking over it stops it immediately), voice picker + speed. - s4 **Connectors + tools**: everything on axHub (github, vps, hostinger, axf-console, amberx...) available with the same approvals/veto flow; tool calls shown as collapsible cards; Follow Amber/console_show hooks. - s5 **Crew link**: talk to Amber and the crew from the chat - queue/stop builds, check status, slot queue, UI Review approve/deny, banners; handoff to Amber. - s6 **Projects + memory**: projects with instructions + files, memory read/write on axHub (same files Amber uses), per-chat model choice (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku), budget caps. - s7 **Settings**: every setting in one Companion settings screen (model, voice, personality/persona field, notifications, approvals, connectors on/off, memory on/off, privacy, export/delete chats), plus overlay bubble to summon Gizmo anywhere on the phone. - s8 Plugins: companion commands exposed via REST + MCP + CLI (standing rule); other plugins can add tools to Gizmo. - Each step: tests/type-check, phone screenshots, UI Review item. Report `_claude/builds/reports/gizmo-companion.md` with what's done, what's left, whether a new APK install is needed, and the cost so far. THREADS, PR. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker nod…",
